WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.858
Mrs. Lynde, an old friend of Marilla's, had come to Green Gables to visit and discuss the latest town "news," though most people called it gossip.

2
00:00:10.859 --> 00:00:19.035
"I've heard that you started an improvement society, Anne. Is it true?" asked Mrs. Lynde.

3
00:00:19.036 --> 00:00:29.076
"Not really," said Anne, flushing. "I was just talking it over with some friends. Many towns have improvement societies now."

4
00:00:29.077 --> 00:00:37.683
"It's not a good idea," said Mrs. Lynde. "People don't like being improved, Anne."

5
00:00:37.684 --> 00:00:41.389
"We're not improving the people ," said

6
00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:49.164
Anne. "We want to make Avonlea prettier. For instance, we're thinking of painting the town

7
00:00:49.165 --> 00:00:55.133
hall." Mrs. Lynde was unconvinced, but soon the Avonlea Improvement Society was

8
00:00:55.134 --> 00:01:04.399
organized, with Gilbert Blythe as president, Fred Wright as vice-president, Anne Shirley as secretary, and Diana Barry as

9
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:12.229
treasurer. The Improvement Society received some disapproval and a good deal of ridicule from Avonlea's older

10
00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:17.457
citizens. Mr. Wright said a better name for the Society would be the "Dating

11
00:01:17.458 --> 00:01:25.370
Club." Mr. Bell said that he might be willing to paint his barn, but there was no way he'd hang lace curtains in his

12
00:01:25.371 --> 00:01:30.130
stables. Despite these jokes the "Improvers" set to

13
00:01:30.131 --> 00:01:35.149
work. Anne and Diana walked along an Avonlea road, visiting each

14
00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:40.380
house. They were collecting donations for the Improvement Society to paint the town

15
00:01:40.381 --> 00:01:45.379
hall. Their first stop was the home of Catherine and Eliza

16
00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:52.453
Andrews. "If Catherine is here, we might get some money," said Diana, "but if Eliza is there, we

17
00:01:52.454 --> 00:01:56.459
won't." Eliza Andrews answered the door, looking very

18
00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:00.703
grim. As the girls explained their errand, Catherine came to the

19
00:02:00.704 --> 00:02:05.687
door. Eliza listened with a frown, but Catherine

20
00:02:05.688 --> 00:02:11.856
smiled. "I won't give any money for that hall, not a cent," said Eliza

21
00:02:11.857 --> 00:02:15.024
sourly. "It's just a place for young people to

22
00:02:15.025 --> 00:02:20.254
meet. Young people should stay at home. This world is getting worse every

23
00:02:20.255 --> 00:02:25.083
day!" "I think it's getting better!" said Catherine

24
00:02:25.084 --> 00:02:31.758
firmly. Eliza changed the subject. "How are Marilla's eyes, Anne? Is she blind

25
00:02:31.759 --> 00:02:36.241
yet?" "Her eyes aren't any worse," Anne replied

26
00:02:36.242 --> 00:02:43.250
meekly. Anne and Diana left disappointed, but as they headed down the road a woman ran up behind

27
00:02:43.251 --> 00:02:47.587
them. It was Catherine Andrews with a dollar in her

28
00:02:47.588 --> 00:02:54.337
hand. "Good luck with the Improvement Society!" she said. The girls cheered

29
00:02:54.338 --> 00:03:02.111
up. Their next visit was to Mrs. Bell, who looked very healthy but spent a half an hour describing all her aches and

30
00:03:02.112 --> 00:03:09.980
pains. Mrs. Bell gave them money but said she couldn't donate next year because she would probably be in her grave by

31
00:03:09.981 --> 00:03:12.703
then. The worst reception was at the

32
00:03:12.704 --> 00:03:20.536
Fletchers'. Anne and Diana saw two faces in the window as they walked up to the door, but when Anne knocked, nobody

33
00:03:20.537 --> 00:03:24.869
answered. Eventually the Improvers raised enough money to paint the

34
00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:32.037
hall. They decided on dark green and asked Mr. Joshua Pye, an uncle of Anthony Pye, to paint it.

35
00:03:32.038 --> 00:03:40.078
They had to give the contract to a member of the Pye family, or else none of the four Pye families would donate any money.

36
00:03:40.079 --> 00:03:47.290
Mr. Roger Pye brought the hall paint home that night, and Mr. Joshua Pye began painting the next day.

37
00:03:47.291 --> 00:03:50.545
He was not disturbed in his task.

38
00:03:50.546 --> 00:03:58.197
The hall was so closely surrounded by a wood of fir trees that it was invisible to anyone not driving right by it.

39
00:03:58.198 --> 00:04:03.944
Mr. Joshua Pye finished his job Friday afternoon and went home to Carmody.

40
00:04:03.945 --> 00:04:07.379
Later Mrs. Lynde drove by the hall.

41
00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:12.993
She was curious to see what the hall looked like in its new coat of paint.

42
00:04:12.994 --> 00:04:22.811
When Mrs. Lynde rounded the curve and saw the brilliant blue town hall, she dropped the reins and said, "Good gracious!"

43
00:04:22.812 --> 00:04:29.424
She stared for a moment and then laughed hysterically.

44
00:04:29.425 --> 00:04:33.174
News of the mistake quickly spread through Avonlea.

45
00:04:33.175 --> 00:04:44.039
"Oh, it's simply dreadful!" Anne exclaimed. "I just can't believe Joshua Pye has gone and painted the hall blue instead of green.

46
00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:48.714
It's the blue that people use to paint carts and wheelbarrows.

47
00:04:48.715 --> 00:04:54.740
And Mrs. Lynde says it's the most hideous color for a building that she's ever seen."

48
00:04:54.741 --> 00:04:59.190
"How on earth could such a mistake have happened?" asked Diana.

49
00:04:59.191 --> 00:05:03.810
The blame for this disaster was eventually pinned on the Pyes.

50
00:05:03.811 --> 00:05:07.562
The shades of paint were selected from a numbered color card.

51
00:05:07.563 --> 00:05:13.789
The Improvers had chosen the color number 147 and had told Roger Pye.

52
00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:20.362
However, Roger had somehow bought color number 157 instead.

53
00:05:20.363 --> 00:05:27.147
"I must cry, even if I am almost 17 years old, Marilla," Anne later sobbed.

54
00:05:27.148 --> 00:05:32.951
"It is so embarrassing—people will think the Improvement Society is a joke.

55
00:05:32.952 --> 00:05:38.129
They'll never again listen to our ideas or give us donations."

56
00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:43.907
In life, however, things often turn out differently from how we expect.

57
00:05:43.908 --> 00:05:48.859
The Avonlea people did not laugh at the Improvement Society.

58
00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:54.532
They had donated money to have the town hall painted, and they were angry about the mistake.

59
00:05:54.533 --> 00:06:02.602
Public indignation centered on the Pyes. People felt that Joshua Pye should have realized it was the wrong color.

60
00:06:02.603 --> 00:06:12.218
Joshua Pye argued that he painted the hall the color he was given, and it wasn't his job to question the Improvement Society's taste in color.

61
00:06:12.219 --> 00:06:19.073
Despite Joshua Pye's arguments, the people of Avonlea still took the Improvement Society's side.

62
00:06:19.074 --> 00:06:26.256
People believed the Improvers had worked hard, and many of them took inspiration from the Society's example.

63
00:06:26.257 --> 00:06:34.042
Mr. Major Spencer said he would plant flowers around the town, and Mr. Bell decided to paint his old barn.

64
00:06:34.043 --> 00:06:38.314
Anne, however, was still upset about the town hall.

65
00:06:38.315 --> 00:06:45.648
"Never mind, Anne," Marilla consoled her. "Most paint fades uglier over time.

66
00:06:45.649 --> 00:06:52.065
But that blue started out as ugly as it can be. So it's bound to fade prettier."

67
00:06:52.066 --> 00:07:02.727
Anne smiled, but she was not convinced.

